# Documentation Standards Rule

## ⚠️ CRITICAL: CODE DOCUMENTATION ONLY

**Documentation = inline code documentation only. NO separate .md files unless explicitly requested.**

- ❌ **NEVER create NEW .md files** (README, guides, tutorials, etc.)
- ✅ **Update EXISTING .md files only if they exist**
- ✅ **Create .md files ONLY when explicitly instructed**

## ONLY ALLOWED: Inline Documentation
- ✅ File header comments/docstrings
- ✅ Function/method/class docstrings
- ✅ Inline code comments
- ✅ JSDoc comments for TypeScript/JavaScript
- ✅ Python docstrings
- ✅ Multi-line comment blocks within code files

## Required Documentation Elements
- Module purpose and rationale (in file header)
- Key responsibilities (main functions/classes)
- Usage context (when/how to use)
- Function parameters and return values
- Complex algorithm explanations
- Non-obvious implementation details
- TODOs for known limitations or future improvements

## Enforcement
- All new code files must include inline documentation
- Update inline documentation when files are modified
- "Documentation" = inline code comments/docstrings only
